  "body": "## What changed\n\n- add one reusable styled `AppSelect` and replace the native selects used by Runtime, bot filters, dictionary creation and dictionary management\n- render dropdown menus through a portal so they are not clipped by scroll containers; keep them inside the viewport and automatically open upward when there is not enough space below\n- add a restrained commercial UI layer with consistent spacing, radii, input sizing, focus states, cards, buttons and responsive safety rules\n- make the desktop sidebar collapse into a compact sticky mobile navigation below 980px\n- make Runtime filters responsive and convert the wide Runtime table into labeled cards on smaller screens\n- make the Bots table convert into labeled cards instead of relying on horizontal scrolling on small devices\n- make bot filter forms scale 3 columns -> 2 columns -> 1 column and keep selected-model pricing/reference information readable\n- rebuild `Dodaj model` as a stable 2-column form that becomes one column on narrow screens so help text and labels stay readable\n- rebuild model-management rows so category / edit / delete controls do not drift or overflow as the viewport narrows\n- keep existing Price Matrix responsive behavior and add outer overflow safeguards\n- polish form action layouts, long text handling and scrollbars\n\n## Design intent\n\nThis deliberately stays close to FlipBot's existing visual language: neutral navy/white admin UI, subtle borders and shadows, no flashy gradients, no unnecessary animations and no decorative features that would make the product feel like a different app.\n\n## Responsive behavior\n\n- desktop: current sidebar/table-first workflow remains\n- <=1240px: dense 3-column forms reduce to 2 columns\n- <=980px: sidebar becomes mobile navigation; Runtime/Bots tables become cards; dictionary management stacks cleanly\n- <=740px: forms and filter/reference grids become one column\n- <=520px: actions and card fields stack vertically for phone widths\n\n## Safety / scope\n\n- frontend only\n- no backend, database or Playwright changes\n- no negotiation logic changes\n- no real-action flag, offer limit or submit behavior changes\n\n## Review notes\n\n- branch is based directly on current `main` (`e33d5fe99e2f212894a6c29e6f88a47ff9d17be7`) and is not behind main\n- existing Price Matrix and Market Observer component-specific responsive CSS remain intact\n- `EditBotPage` automatically receives the same bot-filter improvements because it reuses `BotFiltersSection`\n- current `main` contains a pre-existing import of `./pages/HistoryPage` in `App.tsx`, while that file is absent from the GitHub tree; this PR does not invent or modify that unrelated missing page\n- local npm build/browser execution was not available in the assistant environment; GitHub status checks will be inspected before merge",
